<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<topic id="85482458-faf3-4de0-95c0-ef0b3709a1ea" revisionNumber="1">
  <developerHowToDocument
    xmlns="http://ddue.schemas.microsoft.com/authoring/2003/5"
    xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink">



    <section>
      <content>
        <para>
          To configure schedulers using a standard .NET configuration file, the first thing
          you need in your .config file is a <legacyBold>configuration section</legacyBold>.
        </para>
        <para>
          The section will contain one or more blocks for each scheduler you need in your
          application. A sample section is shown below.
        </para>

        <code language="xml">
          &lt;configSections&gt;
            &lt;section name=&quot;scheduling&quot; type=&quot;DemiCode.Scheduling.Configuration.SchedulerSettings, DemiCode.Scheduling, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=069d10bcdee4c3e4&quot; /&gt;
          &lt;/configsections&gt;
          &lt;scheduling defaultScheduler=&quot;schedulerName&quot;&gt;
            &lt;!-- ... --&gt;
          &lt;/scheduling&gt;
        </code>

        <para/>
        Assuming the above configuration is placed in your application .config file, the following code will load the configuration and return an initialized scheduler.

        <code language="c#">
          using (Scheduler scheduler = SchedulerFactory.CreateFromConfig("scheduling"))
          {
            // ... start scheduler processing
          }
        </code>

        <para/>
        The same configuration section can be placed in an arbitrary .config file. Assuming this file is called Schedulersettings.config, the following code will load the configuration from that file.

        <code language="c#">
          using (Scheduler scheduler = SchedulerFactory.CreateFromConfigFile(".\\Schedulersettings.config", "scheduling"))
          {
            // ... start scheduler processing
          }
        </code>
      </content>
    </section>

    <section>
      <title>Attributes and Elements</title>
      <content>
        <table>
          <title>Attributes</title>
          <tableHeader>
            <row>
              <entry>
                Attribute
              </entry>
              <entry>
                Description
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tableHeader>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <legacyBold>name</legacyBold>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              Name of the section. This value must correspond to an xml element in the configuration
              file.
            </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <legacyBold>type</legacyBold>
            </entry>
            <entry>
              <para>
                This is the fully qualified class name of the type that handles section
                loading.
              </para>
              <para>
                To use the built-in <codeEntityReference qualifyHint="false">T:DemiCode.Scheduling.Configuration.SchedulerSettings</codeEntityReference> section handler use the following value:<para/>
                <legacyBold>DemiCode.Scheduling.Configuration.SchedulerSettings, DemiCode.Scheduling, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=069d10bcdee4c3e4</legacyBold>
              </para>
            </entry>
          </row>
        </table>

        <table>
          <title>Elements</title>
          <tableHeader>
            <row>
              <entry>Element</entry>
              <entry>Description</entry>
            </row>
          </tableHeader>
          <row>
            <entry>
              <legacyBold>
                <link xlink:href="0ad38964-0c44-4e15-86aa-0a121c1741af">scheduling</link>
              </legacyBold>
            </entry>
            <entry>

              Root element for the scheduling configuration section. The actual name of this element
              could be changed specifying a different name in the &lt;section&gt; element.

            </entry>
          </row>
        </table>
      </content>
    </section>


    <relatedTopics>
    </relatedTopics>

  </developerHowToDocument>
</topic>
